is just highlight some of the
improved areas of performance,

00:39:44.970 --> 00:39:46.410
some of which we've touched on,

00:39:46.410 --> 00:39:48.690
some of the more challenged
areas from last month,

00:39:48.690 --> 00:39:51.750
and then just end with some
of the key operational metrics

00:39:51.750 --> 00:39:54.180
from our last published set of data.

00:39:54.180 --> 00:39:55.770
So in terms of improved performance,

00:39:55.770 --> 00:39:57.570
we've touched on a number
of these areas already,

00:39:57.570 --> 00:40:01.020
but pleasing to see the
number of adult inpatients

00:40:01.020 --> 00:40:03.720
who have autistic or learning disability

00:40:03.720 --> 00:40:06.000
continue to decrease,

00:40:06.000 --> 00:40:09.480
positive to see mental
health bed days out of area,

00:40:09.480 --> 00:40:11.550
a point that was mentioned earlier,

00:40:11.550 --> 00:40:14.640
continue to decrease actually nearly 10%

00:40:14.640 --> 00:40:18.240
when looked at so similar
performance levels last year.

00:40:18.240 --> 00:40:19.230
The percentage of patients

00:40:19.230 --> 00:40:22.170
conveyed to emergency
departments by ambulances

00:40:22.170 --> 00:40:24.270
continue to decrease marginally,

00:40:24.270 --> 00:40:25.380
but it's important we're seeing

00:40:25.380 --> 00:40:27.930
that that trend starting to fall down.

00:40:27.930 --> 00:40:29.490
And on particular clinical areas

00:40:29.490 --> 00:40:31.380
like diabetes care processes,

00:40:31.380 --> 00:40:32.460
we are seeing against

00:40:32.460 --> 00:40:34.680
the eight NICE recommended processes,

00:40:34.680 --> 00:40:36.600
continued improvement both for type 1

00:40:36.600 --> 00:40:39.090
and type 2 diabetics.

00:40:39.090 --> 00:40:40.110
We mentioned earlier

00:40:40.110 --> 00:40:44.940
the continued improvement on
the percentage of patients

00:40:44.940 --> 00:40:48.360
finding it easier to contact
their general practitioner,

00:40:48.360 --> 00:40:53.360
and you'll see that that figure
is now up to just over 73%.

00:40:53.970 --> 00:40:56.310
We are continuing to see a decrease

00:40:56.310 --> 00:41:00.270
in children being prescribed
antibiotics inappropriately,

00:41:00.270 --> 00:41:01.470
and we'll come on to pick up

00:41:01.470 --> 00:41:05.700
some of the other key operational
areas as we move down.

00:41:05.700 --> 00:41:08.160
Very finally, on areas of success,

00:41:08.160 --> 00:41:09.210
the children and young people

00:41:09.210 --> 00:41:13.560
accessing NHS mental health
services continues to rise.

00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:16.830
But I think in the theme
that Jim said earlier,

00:41:16.830 --> 00:41:18.090
this is an area where we know

00:41:18.090 --> 00:41:20.010
we are seeing modest improvement,

00:41:20.010 --> 00:41:21.570
but we all know is an area

00:41:21.570 --> 00:41:23.310
where we are absolutely focused

00:41:23.310 --> 00:41:26.160
on continued improvement
and dramatic delivery,

00:41:26.160 --> 00:41:28.770
which is something we
need to do moving forward.

00:41:28.770 --> 00:41:30.960
And finally, a modest improvement again

00:41:30.960 --> 00:41:32.910
in community mental health access rate,

00:41:32.910 --> 00:41:34.830
which I think sits into the same theme

00:41:34.830 --> 00:41:36.720
that I was just mentioning.

00:41:36.720 --> 00:41:39.090
So a lot of other positive
areas within the pack,

00:41:39.090 --> 00:41:40.710
but those are hopefully
some of the highlight

00:41:40.710 --> 00:41:44.066
that cut across different care settings

00:41:44.066 --> 00:41:46.770
and affect our population
in different ways.

00:41:46.770 --> 00:41:48.450
So there are a number of challenged areas

00:41:48.450 --> 00:41:50.520
where our performance has not improved

00:41:50.520 --> 00:41:52.980
either against last month's performance,

00:41:52.980 --> 00:41:55.470
but more importantly, last year.

00:41:55.470 --> 00:41:57.060
And disappointing to see levels

00:41:57.060 --> 00:42:00.780
of cervical screening slightly decrease

00:42:00.780 --> 00:42:02.760
when compared against previous figures

00:42:02.760 --> 00:42:03.630
a couple of years ago.

00:42:03.630 --> 00:42:05.547
So it is an area and we may well come

00:42:05.547 --> 00:42:08.070
and talk about screening more generally

00:42:08.070 --> 00:42:11.580
that we need to see a
continued area of focus.

00:42:11.580 --> 00:42:15.720
MMR vaccine uptake certainly compared

00:42:15.720 --> 00:42:17.550
to a couple of years ago

00:42:17.550 --> 00:42:20.130
still stands now about 83%,

00:42:20.130 --> 00:42:22.920
which puts us outside of
the recommended levels

00:42:22.920 --> 00:42:24.303
for a developed country.

00:42:25.410 --> 00:42:27.780
And that brings us probably on

00:42:27.780 --> 00:42:30.780
to some of the key operational
performance metrics,

00:42:30.780 --> 00:42:35.460
just finally, so UEC elective
cancer and diagnostics.

00:42:35.460 --> 00:42:38.070
And again, slightly confusingly I know,

00:42:38.070 --> 00:42:41.190
but the data for UEC
is driven from December

00:42:41.190 --> 00:42:42.930
and the data for elective and cancer

00:42:42.930 --> 00:42:45.990
is driven from the
published data of November.

00:42:45.990 --> 00:42:48.420
But colleagues of course may
have more up-to-date data

00:42:48.420 --> 00:42:49.950
that they may be able to share.

00:42:49.950 --> 00:42:51.783
So just firstly on UEC,

00:42:53.580 --> 00:42:55.400
there was an average,
just to remind everyone,

00:42:55.400 --> 00:42:59.970
of about 75,000 attendances per day.

00:42:59.970 --> 00:43:01.830
So demand, however, for services,

00:43:01.830 --> 00:43:03.390
has decreased ever so slightly

00:43:03.390 --> 00:43:06.240
when you look at this month last year.

00:43:06.240 --> 00:43:08.010
Ambulance instancees continue

00:43:08.010 --> 00:43:10.050
to reach almost 30,000 a year,

00:43:10.050 --> 00:43:12.840
which is an increase from
the same time last year.

00:43:12.840 --> 00:43:14.250
And four-hour performance,

00:43:14.250 --> 00:43:17.430
when last published was at 73.8%,

00:43:17.430 --> 00:43:19.200
which when looked against last year,

00:43:19.200 --> 00:43:22.620
is a 2.7 percentage point increase.

00:43:22.620 --> 00:43:24.990
So something that I think
reflects earlier conversation

00:43:24.990 --> 00:43:27.150
and how hard people are working.

00:43:27.150 --> 00:43:30.720
The percentage of patients
spending over 12 hours in A&amp;E

00:43:30.720 --> 00:43:34.830
is reducing ever so
slightly since last month,

00:43:34.830 --> 00:43:37.980
but has improved again
compared to last year.

00:43:37.980 --> 00:43:39.480
And finally as mentioned earlier,

00:43:39.480 --> 00:43:41.940
category two mean ambulance performance

00:43:41.940 --> 00:43:44.610
was 32 minutes just over,

00:43:44.610 --> 00:43:46.647
which is a few seconds faster than before,

00:43:46.647 --> 00:43:50.340
but about 14 minutes
faster than a year ago.

00:43:50.340 --> 00:43:51.600
So probably matches

00:43:51.600 --> 00:43:53.850
exactly the conversation
we were just having.

00:43:53.850 --> 00:43:55.290
We are looking at elective,

00:43:55.290 --> 00:43:57.630
and the published data for November.

00:43:57.630 --> 00:44:01.880
Our waiting list has decreased
down by almost 86,000

00:44:01.880 --> 00:44:06.600
to the previous month and
170,000 from last year.

00:44:06.600 --> 00:44:08.010
And of those waiting,

00:44:08.010 --> 00:44:12.060
nearly 62% were waiting
less than 18 weeks.

00:44:12.060 --> 00:44:14.730
The proportion of 52-wait week waiters

00:44:14.730 --> 00:44:16.950
was 2.1% in November.

00:44:16.950 --> 00:44:19.950
So again an improvement
on our position last year

00:44:19.950 --> 00:44:22.260
as we work at attacking the
tail of the waiting list

00:44:22.260 --> 00:44:24.960
and the bulk of the
waiting list in the middle.

00:44:24.960 --> 00:44:26.850
Final two areas of focus, if I may,

00:44:26.850 --> 00:44:30.760
cancer, where performance
against the FDS standard

00:44:32.040 --> 00:44:33.990
was higher when compared to last month,

00:44:33.990 --> 00:44:37.350
but sadly ever so slightly
lower than the previous year,

00:44:37.350 --> 00:44:41.430
and I know is an area of
particular focus for all systems.

00:44:41.430 --> 00:44:45.990
And then performance against
the 62-day standard was 70.2%,

00:44:45.990 --> 00:44:48.030
which is higher than last month

00:44:48.030 --> 00:44:50.970
and higher than our previous year.

00:44:50.970 --> 00:44:53.100
Finally on diagnostics,

00:44:53.100 --> 00:44:56.400
nearly 22% of patients
waited over six weeks,

00:44:56.400 --> 00:44:58.080
which is slightly worse than last month,

00:44:58.080 --> 00:44:59.417
and slightly worse than last year.

00:44:59.417 --> 00:45:01.830
And of course the diagnostic pathway

00:45:01.830 --> 00:45:05.400
impacts the cancer pathway clearly.

00:45:05.400 --> 00:45:08.070
So very happy, Penny, to take questions,

00:45:08.070 --> 00:45:09.510
and as I say, colleagues around the table

00:45:09.510 --> 00:45:10.980
as well very close to this.

