that Duncan raised,

00:54:26.280 --> 00:54:27.990
and what we think is working,

00:54:27.990 --> 00:54:30.963
are we on a good progress
there that would be helpful?

00:54:32.700 --> 00:54:34.560
I'd like to pick up community waits.

00:54:34.560 --> 00:54:35.520
Those are not good,

00:54:35.520 --> 00:54:37.800
we don't really talk about it that much.

00:54:37.800 --> 00:54:40.500
We know we've got some big
productivity challenges there.

00:54:40.500 --> 00:54:42.050
How are we going to get into that?

00:54:42.960 --> 00:54:45.370
I was disappointed to see
sickness absence is up

00:54:46.440 --> 00:54:49.010
when we've got a big focus
on trying to get it down.

00:54:49.010 --> 00:54:50.910
So what are we doing on that?

00:54:50.910 --> 00:54:52.920
And then Ravi's question

00:54:52.920 --> 00:54:57.090
on how quickly do we think
elective waits can come down?

00:54:57.090 --> 00:54:59.970
We had good having lots of
conversations about that

00:54:59.970 --> 00:55:01.200
and we'll have more this afternoon,

00:55:01.200 --> 00:55:03.300
but it would be good to talk about that.

00:55:03.300 --> 00:55:05.190
- Yeah, I'll take back what I said before

00:55:05.190 --> 00:55:06.585
by the way.
- There you go.

00:55:10.026 --> 00:55:11.360
- Thanks, thanks Penny.

00:55:11.360 --> 00:55:15.570
So firstly, on all the comments
from you and colleagues,

00:55:15.570 --> 00:55:18.210
