is from the National
Diabetes Audit, not from QOF,

00:55:50.580 --> 00:55:52.770
which is why I think last time you met it,

00:55:52.770 --> 00:55:53.820
it appeared they got worse.

00:55:53.820 --> 00:55:55.680
We've got just by actually

00:55:55.680 --> 00:55:56.820
taking the quarterly data

00:55:56.820 --> 00:55:59.020
rather than the annual
data, it's different.

00:56:00.240 --> 00:56:02.430
We've got the modern service
framework that's coming out

00:56:02.430 --> 00:56:03.750
and we've got the discussion later on

00:56:03.750 --> 00:56:04.830
this afternoon about neighbourhoods.

00:56:04.830 --> 00:56:06.570
And one of the things that
neighbourhoods will do

00:56:06.570 --> 00:56:08.850
and has to do is improve the management

00:56:08.850 --> 00:56:12.180
of long-term conditions and
multiple long-term conditions.

00:56:12.180 --> 00:56:13.650
I think the modern service framework

00:56:13.650 --> 00:56:15.630
will show us that case
finding of hypertension

00:56:15.630 --> 00:56:18.150
will be one of the things that
will have the biggest impact

00:56:18.150 --> 00:56:20.190
on improving life expectancy

00:56:20.190 --> 00:56:21.600
as well as improving outcomes.

00:56:21.600 --> 00:56:23.130
So we need to think

00:56:23.130 --> 00:56:25.470
about how we manage long-term
conditions differently

00:56:25.470 --> 00:56:27.720
about how secondary care works
differently with primary care

00:56:27.720 --> 00:56:30.270
and not actually also how we do

00:56:30.270 --> 00:56:32.010
